================================================================================
=== Program VSP-METIS.sh (main program) ========================================
================================================================================
First argument must be the directory where the problems are located
problems.txt should contain the file names, one per line

Second argument (optional) is the random number generator seed. If one is not
provided, then a random number is generated

WARNING: path must include a trailing backslash

Example
./VSP-METIS.sh /home/ovi/data/symmetric/
./VSP-METIS.sh /media/hager/datafile/symmetric/

================================================================================
=== Data Description ===========================================================
================================================================================
All symmetrix and pattern symmetric matrices from SuiteSparse, excluding
matrices corresponding to complete graphs and duplicates.

Duplicates were found and deleted using fdupe

all.txt            - contains all these matrices
int32-n-sorted.txt - subset of matrices whose nz fits in a 32-bit int, sorted
                     in increasing order of the number of vertices
int64-n-sorted.txt - subset of matrices whose nz does not fit in a 32-bit
			         int. That is, the nz is larger than about 2.1 billion

================================================================================
=== Program vsp-metis ==========================================================
================================================================================
    Building:
Pass define INT_TYPE as 32 if you want 32-bit integers.
Otherwise, it defaults to 64-bit integers. You should name the executable
accordingly

    Input:
When running, give the absolute path of the hager6 matrix file as the first
argument

    Output:
Appends the following to output/results.csv
Num Vtx   : X
Num Edges : X
Separator : X
Imbalance : X
Time      : X
(newline)
(newline)

Appends to output/hr_results.txt
